    {
      "body": "<p>This page summarizes all parts and collections submitted in this project. <strong>Deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA)</strong> and <strong>ribonucleic acid (RNA)</strong> are the nucleic acids represented in the sequence entries. In the tables, <strong>complementary DNA (cDNA)</strong> and <strong>coding sequence (CDS)</strong> describe sequence categories; <strong>homologous recombination (HR)</strong> and <strong>clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats–CRISPR-associated protein 9 (CRISPR-Cas9)</strong> describe genome-engineering methods; <strong>single-guide RNA (sgRNA)</strong> and <strong>guide RNA (gRNA)</strong> denote guide molecules; <strong>superfolder green fluorescent protein (sfGFP)</strong> is a localization reporter. The chassis species is <strong><em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</em> (<em>S.c</em>)</strong>; <strong><em>Escherichia coli</em> (<em>E. coli</em>)</strong> is used for plasmid propagation.</p>",
      "_template": "text"
    },
